## Slide 8 — The one underlying mechanism (diagram)
- Layout: Default Slide, Title + Upsubtitle. Upsubtitle: "Same shape, every time". Title: "SXPG_COMMAND_EXECUTE → SM69 → OS sftp/scp".
- Body: BlockProcess or ChevronProcess (4 steps, left to right):
  1. ABAP report
  2. READ zfi_constants (FTP_USER / HOST_KEY / PRIVATE_KEY_PATH / …)
  3. CALL FUNCTION 'SXPG_COMMAND_EXECUTE'
  4. SM69 entry → OS sftp / scp binary → remote endpoint
- Caption under the process: "Every confirmed SFTP report reduces to this pattern."

=====

## Slide 9 — Two auth shapes (block comparison)
- Layout: Default Slide, Title only. Title: "Two auth shapes the migration must support".
- Body: BlockGrid 2 columns, 1 row.
- Block A "Key-based (modern)" — icon Web/Window_Lock. Rich list of constants:
  - FTP_USER, FTP_DOMAIN
  - HOST_KEY, PRIVATE_KEY_PATH, PASSPHRASE
  - Optional: FTP_PORT, FOLDER_PATH, FILE_EXT
  - 13 of 14 direct reports + both wrapper FUGRs
- Block B "Password-based (legacy)" — icon Checkmarks/X_Mark_Box_1 (warning shape). Rich list:
  - FTP_USER, FTP_PSWD, FTP_DOMAIN
  - FTP_PORT, HOST_KEY (still)
  - Only ZSFTP_BNP_PARIBAS is pure password-auth
  - Several others read FTP_PSWD defensively
- Caption block under: "Single-auth replacements would break the BNP password path."

