## Slide 27 — What went well (block list)
- Layout: Default Slide, Title only. Title: "What held up".
- Body: BlockGrid 2 columns × 2 rows. Short blocks with icons.
- Block 1 "Per-stage isolation" — icon Processes/Process_1. One stage per session; artifact on disk before the next.
- Block 2 "Raw-SSE evidence" — icon Documents/Document_Checklist_2. Every claim reproducible from curl/*.sse.
- Block 3 "Lessons captured in-flight" — icon Education/Knowledge. 6 skills + 1 decision + 1 tool-usage skill written during the run.
- Block 4 "Iterative scope expansion" — icon Arrows/Arrows_Expand_1. Three independent scans, each justified by the prior finding.

=====

## Slide 28 — What we'd do differently (block list)
- Layout: Default Slide, Title only. Title: "Lessons for the next run".
- Body: BlockGrid 2 columns × 3 rows, 6 compact blocks with icons.
- Block 1 "English prompts only" — icon Education/Global. "First UA batch wasted ~500k tokens."
- Block 2 "Spell out every SearchSource param" — icon Tasks/Document_Structure. "Don't rely on planning-LLM defaults."
- Block 3 "One scan at a time per destination" — icon Calendars_Timing/Clock_24h. "Stability over wall-clock; 4 parallel scans crashed the backend."
- Block 4 "Never mix SearchObject + SearchSource in one prompt" — icon Checkmarks/X_Mark_Circle_1. "Model picks the wrong one."
- Block 5 "Assert tool availability positively" — icon Checkmarks/Checkmark_Circle_1. "Negative assertions leak tool names and trigger amnesia."
- Block 6 "Add 'exactly ONCE' guards" — icon Calendars_Timing/Clock_24h. "Stops 50× GetIncludesList loops."

=====

## Slide 29 — Methodology validation (process)
- Layout: Default Slide, Title + Upsubtitle. Upsubtitle: "The 5-stage tutorial held up". Title: "Three refinements to fold back".
- Body: BlockProcess 3 steps:
  1. Stage 2b open-ended enumeration is necessary (catches wrapper FMs)
  2. Stage 3 needs ≥2 independent markers (password-only would be missed)
  3. Late sanity scan beyond credential literals (caught the ZDMS_SEND_FILE wrapper)

